        "summary": "Depeg reconciler refused to act (suspicious_drop / mass_tier_flip / mass_action)",
        "description": "The reconcile-stablecoin-depeg sweep opened a circuit breaker (event: depeg_circuit_open, field reason). suspicious_drop: Webacy returned far fewer of our tracked tokens than last sweep, so nothing was written (a vendor outage looks like everyone recovering; the advisory set is frozen). mass_tier_flip: too many tracked tokens changed tier in one poll, snapshots were stored but no advisories were touched. mass_action: more than maxActionsPerRun actions were due; the cap was applied and the rest deferred. Either a real market-wide event (act by hand) or a Webacy data incident (do not override until confirmed). Re-run with ignoreCircuitBreaker only after checking dd.xyz and the raw payload_json.",
